You start each workday with a friendly chat with your colleagues, making sure everyone is focused and ready to get to work. As a Warehouse Operator, you and your team are responsible for ensuring the warehouse operates efficiently. As a Warehouse Operator, you ensure the warehouse runs smoothly by picking orders with a handheld scanner, packing and labelling products, transporting pallets with an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT), wrapping pallets,  checking orders for accuracy, preparing shipments, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

This is what we ask from you:

- You are at least 18 years old and have a VMBO level of education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- You have a good command of the English language;
- You are willing to work in two shifts (06.00-15.00 / 15.00-00.00); 
- You are not allowed to wear metal jewelry, piercings, shoes, belts, phones, or smartwatches;
- You live within commuting distance of Moerdijk and have your own transportation;

Do you enjoy being active and seeing tangible results? Are you looking for a job where you can work more hours by working at different locations? Then this combined role is perfect for you!
We offer you the opportunity to work at both the Designer Outlet Center in Roermond and De Leistert vacation park in Roggel. By combining these two locations, you can expect a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

What will you be doing?

You’ll be working at two different locations, which ensures plenty of variety in your work:

Designer Outlet Center Roermond

- Cleaning streets and plazas with street sweepers and pressure washers;
- Emptying trash cans on the premises;
- Picking up litter;
- Ensuring a clean and well-maintained environment for visitors.

De Leistert Holiday Park (Roggel)

- Cleaning bungalows, vacation homes, and restroom facilities;
- Making beds;
- Cleaning kitchens, bathrooms, bedrooms, and living rooms;
- Dusting and mopping the accommodations;
- Identifying and reporting any defects.

This combination offers a varied job where you work both indoors and outdoors and see the immediate results of your work.

Work Hours

- Outlet Roermond: flexible availability, including weekends;
- De Leistert: Mondays and Fridays between 9:00 AM and 3:00 PM (alternating days) with the possibility of additional work during the week;
- A combination of both locations allows for a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

- You’re a go-getter and enjoy being active;
- You’re available for at least 15 hours per week;
- You’re flexible (including weekends for the outlet);
- You’re available on Mondays and Fridays (for De Leistert);
- You speak Dutch, English, or German;
- Experience in cleaning is a plus, but not required.

- Venlo - 40 uur - € 15,68 per uur 
Are you someone who likes to roll up their sleeves, works accurately and enjoys a dynamic working environment? Then we are looking for you! As a Warehouse Employee, you will work in a modern distribution centre in Venlo, where you and your colleagues are responsible for processing and preparing orders for shipment across Europe and the Middle East. 
What do we offer? 
• A gross hourly wage of €15.68; 
• A full-time position of 40 hours per week; 
• A high chance of receiving a permanent contract; 
• Double pay on Sundays and public holidays; 
• Travel allowance of €0.21 per kilometre; 
• Flexible day shifts between 07:00 and 19:00; 
• 30% overtime allowance; 
• 200% pay on Sundays; 
• Paid training and plenty of opportunities for personal and professional development; 
• Working in a modern and sustainable distribution centre in Venlo; 
• An international and dynamic working environment; 
• Access to an exclusive Sample Sale featuring well-known fashion brands. 
What will you do? 
As a Warehouse Employee, you are an important part of the logistics process. 
Your responsibilities will include: - Picking and processing orders for customers across Europe and the Middle East; - Picking fashion items in the warehouse; - Moving and processing goods within the warehouse; - Checking orders and preparing them for shipment; - Identifying and reporting discrepancies and quality issues; - Working together with colleagues and supervisors to ensure orders are processed correctly and on time; - Keeping the workplace clean and safe; - Working according to applicable safety and quality regulations. 
What do you bring? - You are willing to work weekends; - You speak and understand English, as this is the main language spoken on the work floor; - You are motivated, reliable and hardworking; - You work accurately and have an eye for quality; - Experience in logistics is a plus, but motivation and a good work ethic are...
